editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-44.md:101:A boy with no Path, it said, a boy the Compact's own registry had looked at and written down as nothing, had put a Bronze Rank 1 on the ground in a yard in a district at the bottom of a hill somewhere down the river. The boy had done it, the story said, with his bare hands and nothing else. It had been told by a man who had heard it from a man who had been on the river, and by the time it reached Reydan it had grown a crowd of a thousand, and a sword, and a broken arm that nobody could afterward account for.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-49.md:1:# Chapter 49 — Ansel's Round
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-47.md:1:# Chapter 47 — It Compresses Inward
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-47.md:171:The heavyset man's wife began leaving a covered bowl on the range for him at night, without being asked and without saying so. He found it there after the evening hour with Lira, still warm, with a plate over it. On the second night the sister had written on the plate in chalk, *EAT, L SAYS*, and drawn a hen.
